# Cursor Rules, {{MODULE_NAME}}

## Project

Drupal 10/11 custom module `{{MODULE_NAME}}` for {{CLIENT}}.

- Module path: `{{MODULE_PATH}}/`
- DDEV site: `{{DDEV_URL}}` (PHP 8.3, nginx-fpm)

## Agent Resources

Use proactively, do not wait to be asked:

- **drupal-localgov**, Drupal 10/11 + LocalGov workflows (modules, theming, site building, ops).
- **drupal-expert**, correct Drupal API, hook, pattern, or contrib option before non-trivial code.
- **ddev-expert**, DDEV container/config/service troubleshooting.
- **drupal-reviewer**, run after EVERY Drupal PHP file is written or modified.

## Running Commands

Always use DDEV from the repo root. Never run php/drush/composer directly.

```bash
ddev drush <command>
ddev composer <command>
```

## PHP Standards

- PHP 8.3: typed properties, constructor property promotion, `declare(strict_types=1)` in every file
- `final` on service and form classes unless inheritance is required
- PHP attributes for plugins (`#[Block(...)]`), never `@Block` annotations
- Dependency injection always; never `\Drupal::service()` inside a class
- Config schema for all custom config; cache metadata on all render arrays
- Parameterised queries only; sanitise all output

## Working Rules

- Work incrementally and test as you go.
- PHP changes ship with PHPUnit tests; run phpcbf then phpcs before done.
- No em dashes. No code comments unless essential.
